From 13457a275805846bc4328f4de272d8e265485d5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lizhilong <lizhilong22@huawei.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:54:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/71] fix(smap): add extern C declaration for iterate_dir to
 fix aarch64 link error

The iterate_dir function is declared in depends/include/linux/fs.h
without extern "C" wrapping, causing C++ name mangling mismatch
when referenced from test_case_iomem.cpp on aarch64.
Add explicit extern "C" declaration to ensure correct C linkage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/smap/test/tiering/test_case_iomem.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/plugins/smap/test/tiering/test_case_iomem.cpp b/plugins/smap/test/tiering/test_case_iomem.cpp
index 4511d49..50acdf9 100644
--- a/plugins/smap/test/tiering/test_case_iomem.cpp
+++ b/plugins/smap/test/tiering/test_case_iomem.cpp
@@ -791,6 +791,7 @@ TEST_F(IomemTest, IncObmmDevSeqIncrement)
 
 extern "C" int iterate_obmm_dev_dir(void);
 extern "C" long PTR_ERR(const void *ptr);
+extern "C" int iterate_dir(struct file *, struct dir_context *);
 
 TEST_F(IomemTest, IterateObmmDevDirOpenFail)
 {
-- 
